From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: apr: register the GPR callback before probe

apr_device_probe() set the service callback only after the driver's probe
returned, so gpr_do_rx_callback() dropped every reply a GPR service got
during its own probe. q6apm asks the SPF for its state there, so it always
waited out the 5 s command timeout before the sound card could register,
with the SPF long ready. Register the callback before probe and clear it
again if probe fails.
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/apr.c
@@ -367,9 +367,11 @@
 	struct apr_driver *adrv = to_apr_driver(dev->driver);
 	int ret;
 
+	/* GPR drivers wait for replies during their own probe */
+	adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
 	ret = adrv->probe(adev);
-	if (!ret)
-		adev->svc.callback = adrv->gpr_callback;
+	if (ret)
+		adev->svc.callback = NULL;
 
 	return ret;
 }
